==Strategy==
The best way to deal with this stage is to not let Evil Emperor attack at all. Using [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] (level 40 is a recommended minimum) to chain Emperor so that he gets constantly knocked back with support from units such as [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]] and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier]], you are almost guaranteed to beat the stage before the Oldhorn even arrives on the stage. You may need the normal cat cannon to interrupt evil emperor's attack occasionally, but other than that, this stage is quite trivial if your units are at the expected level threshold.

[[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|Rushers]] excel here when Evil Emperor Cat is alone as the enemy limit is low; here are some examples: [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]], [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]], and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]. Cats with [[:Category:Anti-Relic Cats|Anti-Relic]]/[[:Category:Cats with Surge Immunity|Immune to Surge]] abilities can be of great assistance as well. Although they do not work as well as the previously mentioned Cats, other rusher-class Cats are usable in this stage.

Units that can outrange Evil Emperor Cat also excel here, such as [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] (with several Slow Up [[Talents]]), [[Asiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Assassinlan Pasalan]] with Slow Up Talents, and [[Balaluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Piccolan Pasalan]] with Freeze Up [[Cat Combo|Combos]]. Lastly, some generally good units that can do massive damage to all enemies here are [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] (Speed Up and Money Up Talents are both recommended) and [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]] (Strengthen and Attack Buff Talents are recommended for higher damage). [[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]] are another viable choice if leveled high enough. Their [[Wave Attack]] can deal decent damage to the boss and the peons, not to mention being [[Special Abilities#Immune to Freeze|immune to freeze]] makes them a generally useful unit. [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]], albeit having low health, is also another useful unit, being able to help clear out peons and also snipe the boss. [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapsticks Cats]] are also great to have against the other relics here.

==Abyssal Strategy==
The following lineups are designed to work on their own; however, it is recommended and encouraged to add to them as you see fit. Certain [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] can dramatically simplify the stage, so don't be afraid to include them alongside these strategies.

