'''Difficulty:''' ★★★★☆

'''Battle:''' Upgrade your wallet, then take care of the first Sir Rel with a combination of iCat, Neo Cutter Cat, and Bullet Train Cat in that order. They will rebound almost immediately thanks to Evil Emperor's boss shockwave, thus dealing with the second Sir Rel and Ginger Snache. Upgrade your wallet again and let the Cat Base tank the third Sir Rel; that way you can more effectively lure Capy and Sir Seal close enough to burst the latter down using Island Cats and Manic Island Cats. Make sure to get the killing blow on Sir Seal using Bullet Train Cat, else your financial status becomes a pressing concern (just like real life)!

Right after Evil Emperor finishes his first attack is when you want to send out Awakened Bahamut Cat. Your melees should hopefully protect him from taking a direct hit from Capy, which would otherwise kill him instantly. Thunderbolt Cannon is here specifically to protect Bahamut if the situation begins to look dire. From this point on, try to prevent Evil Emperor from getting an attack off whilst continuing the chain. It is worth noting that '''Bahamut can survive two attack cycles assuming he's hit by the main attack + the Surge Attack'''. The stage is as good as beaten once Evil Emperor is out of the way.

