'''Difficulty:''' ★★★★☆

'''Battle:''' This run will be an uphill battle to protect your Naala from getting annihilated by Capy. Start the stage by stacking Luxury Bath Cat, Fishman Cat, and Fiend Cat on the Sir Rel while letting the cat base soak up some hits (to better conserve cash). Watch the base HP; once it gets too low, begin pushing forward with Li'l Mohawk Cats and Cat Cactuses. Send in Naala and Doron after Evil Emperor Cat attacks.

The goal to strive for this time around is simple: kill the Capies as fast as humanly possible. They are by far the biggest thorn in your side, and end up putting Naala in constant peril. You need Naala alive to snipe Evil Emperor and knock him back—buying your other attackers some time to get valuable hits in. Cat Mask Doron and Boulder Cat are here as extra protection in the form of spontaneous defense and crowd-control/burst damage. If you can get a good chain going on Evil Emperor, that's usually everything you need to overwhelm the Capies before Oldhorn spawns. You might notice that none of your spammable units have particularly high DPS or good crowd-control vs. Relics, meaning you will need a luxurious amount of space at your disposal to win the war of attrition against Oldhorn.

